# Wireframe: Issue Detail Page (Assignee Change)

**Version**: 1.1.0

## Changelog

| Version | Change |
|---------|--------|
| 1.1.0 | Added Issues List wireframe (pre-existing screen, assignee reflection). Added error state ASCII sketch for Issue Form Modal. |
| 1.0.0 | Initial wireframes for Issue Detail Page and Issue Form Modal (Assignee Change). |

## Screen Inventory

| Screen | Wireframe Section | States |
|--------|------------------|--------|
| Issues List | § Issues List | populated, loading, error |
| Issue Detail Page | § Issue Detail Page | populated, loading, error, success (assignee changed), error (assignee failed) |
| Issue Form Modal (Edit) | § Issue Form Modal | populated, submitting, error |

---

## Purpose & Flow Context

Lets the user view an issue's full details including current assignee, and navigate to the edit form to change the assignee. Entry: click issue from Issues List. Exit: click "Back" to return to Issues List, or click "Edit" to open the Issue Form Modal.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `👤` | User / avatar | `[T]` | Toast notification |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Shared header (logo, nav, user menu) + main container. Regions:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Logo / Nav / UserMenu | Sticky top |
| Main | Issue detail content | Padded container, max-width 1280px |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Issue identifier + title (h1)
2. Metadata bar (status badge, priority, assignee, dates)
3. Description section
4. Comments section

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [< Back]                       [Edit] [Delete]                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  LAG-123                                                           |
|  # Issue Title                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|  [In Progress]  Medium                                            |
|                                                                    |
|  Assignee:  👤 John Doe                                            |
|  Created:   Jan 15, 2026                                          |
|  Updated:   Jul 21, 2026                                          |
|                                                                    |
|  Labels:  [frontend] [Feature]                                     |
|                                                                    |
|  ## Description                                                    |
|  Issue description text here...                                    |
|                                                                    |
|  ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
|                                                                    |
|  ## Comments                                                       |
|  [Comment list...]                                                 |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| [< Back] | Button (ghost) | Navigates to `/issues` | — |
| [Edit] | Button (secondary) | Opens IssueFormModal in edit mode | — |
| [Delete] | Button (danger) | Opens ConfirmDeleteDialog | — |
| Status badge | IssueStatusBadge | Click opens dropdown to change status; shows spinner during API call | Loading state disables interaction |
| Assignee display | `div` text + avatar | Read-only display of current `assigneeName`; no inline edit — use Edit modal | Shows initials avatar or nothing if unassigned |
| Toast | Toast (snackbar) | Appears temporarily after assignee change (success/error) | Auto-dismisses after duration |

## Data Display

Key-value metadata list in the detail view: assignee, created date, updated date. Labels displayed as a tag/badge row.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| "Back" | Navigate to parent list | Consistent with list→detail navigation |
| "Edit" | Open edit modal | User language — "Edit issue" |
| "Assignee" | Label for the assignee field | Human label, not raw `assigneeId` |
| "Assignee updated" (toast) | Confirmation that assign change succeeded | Success feedback |
| "Assignee is not a member of this team" (toast) | Explain why the assign failed | Plain language, no error codes |

## States

### Populated (Default)

The layout shown in the ASCII sketch above. Issue data is loaded and displayed.

### Loading

```  
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [==== skeleton bar ====]                                         |
|                                                                    |
|  [=========================== skeleton bar ======================] |
|  [=========================== skeleton bar ======================] |
|  [==== skeleton bar ====]   [==== skeleton bar ====]              |
|  [==== skeleton bar ====]                                         |
|  [=========================== skeleton bar ======================] |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Error

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [ErrorBanner: "Failed to load issue. Please try again."]        |
|  [Retry]                                                          |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

Error banner with a retry button. Plain-language message.

### Success (Assignee Changed)

A toast appears: `[T] "Assignee updated"` (green/success variant) slides in from bottom-right, auto-dismisses after 3s. Issue detail view reflects new assignee name.

### Error (Assignee Failed)

A toast appears: `[T] "Assignee is not a member of this team"` or `[T] "Failed to update assignee. Please try again."` (red/error variant), auto-dismisses after 5s. Issue detail view reverts to previous assignee.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full layout as described; two-column could show metadata sidebar |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Single column stack; metadata inline |
| Mobile (<768px) | Same single column; buttons stack vertically; touch targets ≥44px |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | h1 → Issue title; h2 → "Description", "Comments" |
| Reading / Focus order | Back → Edit → Delete → Status badge → metadata → description → comments |
| Accessible names | Icon-only Edit/Delete buttons get `aria-label="Edit issue"` / `aria-label="Delete issue"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through all controls; Enter/Space to activate; Escape closes modals |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on all interactive targets |
| Focus not obscured | Sticky header does not overlap focused content |
| Non-color intent | Status uses text + color; priority uses text + icon + color |

---

# Wireframe: Issue Form Modal (Edit / Assignee Change)

## Purpose & Flow Context

Overlay form where the user edits issue fields including the assignee, then submits to save changes. Entry: click "Edit" on the Issue Detail Page. Exit: submit (success → toast + detail page updated) or cancel (→ detail page unchanged).

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: N/A — modal overlay, no grid.

**App-shell**: N/A — modal is a floating overlay.

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Form fields (title, description, status, priority, assignee, labels)
2. Action buttons (Cancel, Save)

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [X]                                                              |
|  # Edit Issue                                                     |
|                                                                    |
|  Title:                                                           |
|  [______________________________________________________________] |
|                                                                    |
|  Description:                                                     |
|  [______________________________________________________________] |
|  [______________________________________________________________] |
|                                                                    |
|  Status:        [>In Progress ▼]                                  |
|  Priority:      [>Medium ▼]                                       |
|  Assignee:      [>John Doe ▼]   or   [>Unassigned ▼]              |
|  Labels:        [frontend] [Feature] [+]                          |
|                                                                    |
|  [Cancel]                                [Save]                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [>Dropdown] [X = Close] [#Heading]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| [X] | Button (ghost) | Closes modal, discards changes | Escape key also closes |
| Title input | `input[type="text"]` | Text field for issue title | Required field |
| Description | `textarea` | Multi-line text | Optional |
| Status dropdown | Select | Dropdown to change status | Pre-filled with current value |
| Priority dropdown | Select | Dropdown to change priority | Pre-filled with current value |
| Assignee dropdown | Select | Dropdown to select assignee or unassign (null) | Options: team members + "Unassigned" to clear |
| Labels | Tag input | Add/remove labels | Existing pattern |
| [Cancel] | Button (secondary) | Closes modal, discards changes | — |
| [Save] | Button (primary) | Submits form; shows spinner while submitting | Disabled during submission |

## Data Display

Form fields pre-filled with existing issue data. Assignee dropdown includes all team members as options, plus "Unassigned" to represent `null`.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| "Edit Issue" | Modal heading | Consistent with "Edit" button label |
| "Assignee" | Label for assignee selector | Human label for `assigneeId` field |
| "Unassigned" | Option to clear assignee | Plain language for `null` |
| "Save" | Submit action | Standard save call-to-action |
| "Cancel" | Dismiss without saving | Standard cancel |

## States

### Populated (Default)

The layout shown in the ASCII sketch. All fields pre-filled with current issue data.

### Submitting

Save button shows spinner, all inputs disabled, modal backdrop remains. No double-submit.

```
|  [Spinner]                                                         |
|  [Cancel]                    [Save ●●●]                            |
```

### Error (Validation)

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [X]                                                              |
|  # Edit Issue                                                     |
|                                                                    |
|  Title:                                                           |
|  [!_____________________________________________________________] |
|  [Title is required]                                              |
|                                                                    |
|  Description:                                                     |
|  [______________________________________________________________] |
|  [______________________________________________________________] |
|                                                                    |
|  Status:        [>In Progress ▼]                                  |
|  Priority:      [>Medium ▼]                                       |
|  Assignee:      [>John Doe ▼]                                     |
|  Labels:        [frontend] [Feature] [+]                          |
|                                                                    |
|  [Cancel]                                [Save]                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
                              [T] "Assignee is not a member of this team"
```

Inline validation highlights required fields with red border + error message below. Business rule errors (422 from assignee endpoint) shown as a toast at bottom, modal stays open so user can correct. Toast auto-dismisses after 5s.

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | N/A — modal dialog |
| Heading order | h2 "Edit Issue" |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus trapped inside modal: header → title → description → status → priority → assignee → labels → Cancel → Save |
| Accessible names | Close button: `aria-label="Close"`; Assignee: `aria-label="Assignee"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab cycles through form fields; Escape closes; Enter submits; Arrow keys for dropdowns |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px |
| Focus not obscured | Modal is centered, no sticky regions inside |
| Non-color intent | N/A |

