# Wireframe: Issues List

## Purpose & Flow Context

Pre-existing list view where the updated assignee is reflected after navigating back from the Issue Detail Page. Entry: click "Back" on Issue Detail Page. Exit: click an issue row → Issue Detail Page. This change adds no structural modifications to the Issues List; assignee reflection is automatic via store cache invalidation (`issues:list` cache invalidated on `assignIssue` success).

**Grid**: 12-column layout (inherits shared shell).
**App-shell**: Shared header + main container (identical to Issue Detail Page shell).

## Layout Regions

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Logo / Nav / UserMenu | Sticky top |
| Main | Issue list table | Padded container, max-width 1280px |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Page title + create button
2. Issue table: checkbox, identifier, title, status badge, priority, assignee, updated date
3. Pagination

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Issues                                                  [New Issue] |
|                                                                     |
|  [] LAG-123  Title text...      [In Progress]  Medium  👤 John Doe  |
|  [] LAG-122  Another issue...   [Backlog]      Low     👤 Jane Doe  |
|  [] LAG-121  Third item...      [Done]         High    —            |
|                                                                     |
|  [< Prev]  1 2 3 ...  [Next >]                                     |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [#Heading] [Table]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Issue row link | `tr` + `a` | Click navigates to `/issues/:id` | — |
| Assignee cell | Avatar + text | Read-only display of `assigneeName`; updates automatically after `assignIssue` via cache invalidation | Shows initials or nothing if unassigned |
| [New Issue] | Button (primary) | Opens Issue Form Create modal | — |
| Pagination | Pagination | Navigate pages | First/last page state |

## Data Display

Table with checkbox, identifier, title, status badge, priority, assignee avatar+name, updated date. Sortable by column (existing pattern). Assignee column auto-reflects changes from the detail page via store cache invalidation — no manual refresh needed.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| "Issues" | Page title | Consistent section heading |
| "New Issue" | Create CTA | Matches existing pattern |
| Assignee display | Read-only name + avatar | Data from issue model, no inline edit |

## States

### Populated (Default)

The table layout shown in the ASCII sketch. All issues loaded with current assignee data.

### Loading

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [=========================== skeleton bar ======================] |
|  [=========================== skeleton bar ======================] |
|  [=========================== skeleton bar ======================] |
|  [=========================== skeleton bar ======================] |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

Skeleton rows mirroring the table structure (5 rows).

### Error

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [ErrorBanner: "Failed to load issues. Please try again."]        |
|  [Retry]                                                          |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

Error banner with retry button. Plain-language message.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full table with all columns |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Single column card list, avatar+name inline |
| Mobile (<768px) | Stacked card layout with key fields; touch targets ≥44px |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | h1 → "Issues" |
| Reading / Focus order | Header nav → New Issue → table rows → pagination |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through controls; Arrow keys navigate table; Enter opens issue |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px |
| Focus not obscured | Sticky header does not overlap focused content |
| Non-color intent | Status + priority use text + icon + color |
